 -- Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@gmail.com>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:30:34 +0300

build-box-utils (0.16.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: build-box-do mounted and unmounted by path as root, which a
    symlink swapped into the target tree could redirect elsewhere. Every
    mount, remount, propagation change and unmount now goes through a
    descriptor to the verified parent directory, and a bind mount keeps
    the flags its source already had when nosuid and friends are added.
  * Fixed: no_new_privs is set after the privilege drop, before anything
    runs inside a target, so a setuid binary placed in the tree runs as
    the user.
  * Fixed: an isolated session left its mounts shared with the host and
    mounted its proc by path. Mounts are made private before the chroot
    and the session's proc is mounted through a descriptor.
  * Fixed: concurrent mount or umount calls on the same target stacked
    mounts. Calls on a target are serialized with a lock on its
    directory; a lock that is not released within five seconds is given
    up on with an error rather than waited for indefinitely.
  * Fixed: a mount was left behind, without its flags and still shared,
    when a step after the mount call failed. It is taken down again.
  * Fixed: a new per-user directory and a new per-target home are created
    0700. Existing ones keep their mode.
  * Fixed: files copied into the target took a symlink's own mode instead
    of the mode of the file behind it. Setuid bits are never copied.
  * Fixed: directories are created natively instead of by running
    mkdir(1) found on the caller's PATH.
  * Fixed: an environment entry without a name made build-box-do spin
    forever; such entries are dropped.
  * Fixed: "build-box delete" did not notice a mount still below a target
    whose path contains a space, tab, newline or backslash, and would
    have removed through it.
  * Fixed: a distro-info failure in "build-box create" was reported as an
    unknown release; "build-box create -c" crashed.
  * Changed: "build-box run" takes its options before the target name
    and passes everything after it to the command as it is, so the
    command may carry options of its own without a separating "--". A
    "--" after the target is still accepted. An option placed after the
    target is no longer read by build-box.
  * Changed: command lines are parsed alike on glibc and musl, and
    POSIXLY_CORRECT in the caller's environment no longer changes how
    build-box-do reads its arguments.
  * Added: a test suite, run during the package build. C and shell tests
    live in tests/c, the privileged paths run inside an unprivileged user
    namespace and skip where none can be created; pytest tests for the
    Python wrapper live in tests/python. Build-Depends now names
    python3-pytest. "./configure --enable-coverage" and "make coverage"
    report line and branch coverage; scripts/musl-build.sh builds and
    tests against musl in a container.

 -- Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@gmail.com>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:11:24 +0300

build-box-utils (0.15.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Changed: the generated aept.conf inside the target now sets
    "clean_cache no", so aept keeps downloaded packages in /.pkg-cache
    instead of purging them after each operation.
  * Changed: the generated aept.conf now sets "ignore_ownership 1",
    since packages are unpacked as an unprivileged user and file
    ownership inside the target cannot be preserved.
  * Fixed: /home inside the sysroot is now created with mode 0755 to
    match what base-files ships. Previously it inherited the umask and
    "aept verify" reported a mode mismatch.

 -- Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@gmail.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 13:13:33 +0300

build-box-utils (0.14.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: host-side scripts in specfiles that invoke aept themselves
    (e.g. `aept --offline-root "$AELTRA_SYSROOT" update`) failed the
    same "'cache_dir' exists but is not a directory" validation that
    0.14.0 fixed for framework-launched aept calls. The framework now
    also injects AEPT_CACHE_DIR into the env of host scripts so their
    own aept invocations pick up the host cache path. Chroot scripts
    do not receive it (they use /.pkg-cache via RealHome as before).
    Requires aept >= 0.4.0 and aeltra-distro-tools >= 1.13.0.

 -- Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@gmail.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 10:28:06 +0300

build-box-utils (0.14.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: chroot activity during target creation could rewrite the
    /.pkg-cache symlink to a RealHome-relative target, invalidating
    the host view and breaking subsequent host-side aept invocations
    with "'cache_dir' exists but is not a directory". The symlink is
    no longer mutated in-chroot; it is created once at prepare time
    pointing through RealHome, and host-side aept bypasses it by
    passing --cache-dir directly. Requires aept >= 0.3.0.
  * Changed: /.pkg-cache is created chroot-relative from the start
    (broken from host view, resolves inside the chroot via the
    RealHome bind mount). Pre-existing targets carrying the old
    host-absolute symlink should be rebuilt.

 -- Tobias Koch <tobias.koch@gmail.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 01:24:38 +0300

